WEBVTT

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:17.350
I can see it now. That's SPES's base.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.600
Where you say this Alicia girl is...

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.730
Our goals are clear-cut:
Subduing Hel and rescuing Alicia.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.940
The fifth heart she harvested
as Jack the Ripper

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.360
has most likely worn down by now
and is no longer functioning.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.740
In short, now is our best chance.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.750
Three years after our battle with
SPES began... this is finally it.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:46.040
Sidekick... Shall I stroke your head?

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:49.210
What was the segue into that?

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.130
Mom, I'm scared.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:55.090
You really are erratic in your moods.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.340
You don't want me to?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.970
Don't be silly. How could I do
something so embarrassing?

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.190
Hmph. I'll give up my place.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.110
Come here.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:13.190
That's quite a dramatic pose
just to offer a head rub.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.990
We've got a little time,
so I thought I'd give you a hug.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:20.240
Don't try to press your chest against
a guy as if it's a commonplace thing.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.990
You have a unique way of
expressing things, Kimi.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:27.080
Okay, fine. Some other time, then.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.750
I doubt that time will come.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:40.510
Hey, you should've taken that hug from
Mom earlier, when you had the chance.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:44.060
That's silly. You think I could
do something so pathetic?

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.600
You'll regret it if you keep being
so obstinate all the time,

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.520
since you have nobody else besides Mom.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.400
That's not... And what's more, Siesta
has nobody else but me either, right?

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.780
She doesn't.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.580
Mom doesn't have anyone but you.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.970
"Episode 9"
"SPES"

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:47.310
There's nobody here.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.140
And here I was mentally prepared
for at least two or three fights.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:05.780
Wha--?

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.630
What are these? Corpses?

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.680
Cerberus? No, you're--

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.640
Sadly for you, I am not Hel.

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.150
Bat?

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:43.610
Ooh, that's a great reaction!
But I'm not Bat either.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:45.950
Then who are you?

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.910
I'm the parent.

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.620
Wait, you're SPES's...

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:58.380
A parent who wantonly kills his children--
your thinking is that of a monster.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:05.430
No. I am neither a person
nor a monster. I am "Seed."

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:08.760
I'm a form of plant life that flew to
this star system from outer space.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.100
What?

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.020
Though I say "plant,"

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.100
that is only if I'm attempting to force us into
classifications as you humans describe them.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.440
Come on, give me a break.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:23.110
What in the world are you telling me
we've been fighting against?

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.820
What are your intentions?

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:30.830
Answer her, Seed. For what purpose
is SPES committing terrorist acts?

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.450
It's for the purpose of surviving.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:42.630
Our intentions are to blanket this
planet with "seeds." Only that.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:52.680
The most primordial drive of living
things is to leave behind offspring.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:58.770
In birthing clones like this,
I wish for my seed to flourish.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:03.400
You think that motive makes it okay
to kill innocent human beings?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.190
What's the matter with
eliminating an alien species

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:10.070
that stands in the way
of spreading our seed?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.740
You're the ones who are an alien species!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.160
Wha--?

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:27.170
The "seeds" of my fallen brethren here
have now been taken in by that one.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:30.430
Hel, you mean? Where is Hel?

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:36.600
She isn't here, which means there's only
one conceivable place she could be, no?

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.730
Kimizuka, Mom!

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.900
Right, I know. Hurry!

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.200
It looks like I'll get
to have my fun, too.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.370
It can't be... Chameleon!

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.590
Kimizuka!

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.810
Let me ride behind you someday.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:28.570
He--Chameleon--said he'd get to
have his fun, <i>too</i>. Which means...

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:29.940
Crap.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.500
Siesta!

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.670
Stop playing around!

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:52.680
You promised you wouldn't go off
and die without a word to us!

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.050
Right?

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.810
Forgive me.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:08.820
I never supposed you
would come here, Kimi.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:15.070
What a mess. My plan has gone awry.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:20.540
The root cause must be that your love
for me was deeper than I supposed.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:25.040
That said, Kimi,
performing first aid is fine,

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:29.800
but normally, checking whether someone
is breathing on their own comes first.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:33.220
You... So your heart was beating
before I started?

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.510
No, it wasn't beating, but--

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.680
It was stopped?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:40.970
I've felt mildly outmatched
against Chameleon.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:44.770
Since it seemed like a hassle, I had
stopped my heart and was playing dead.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:48.230
Stopped... your heart?

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.030
I'm only now asking after
three years together,

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.280
but just what manner of person are you?

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.240
Huh?

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:04.120
Could it be you've gone weak in the
knees with relief, knowing I'm okay?

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:08.080
Can I tell you my honest
feelings right now?

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.960
No! Don't! I won't listen.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.800
I'm thinking you're very cute.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:17.550
Argh! I can't hear a thing!

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.890
What to do... Shall I stroke
your head after all?

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.770
I positively refuse!

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:23.810
Shall I hug you?

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.730
Not a chance.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.440
Or in Kimi-speak,
press my chest against you?

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:32.650
Don't ever so casually try
doing this to any other guy!

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:36.150
Oh, but you touched
my chest earlier already.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.820
This is absurd.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:43.580
Siesta, you've come into my life to
kill me, haven't you? Socially, that is.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:46.960
Teasing you is truly a pleasure, Kimi.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.750
It truly was a pleasure.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.470
Siesta...

00:09:56.970 --> 00:10:01.720
Maybe just once, comfort me
by holding me to your breast.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.810
If we survive to meet again
outside this island, that is. So...

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:15.150
Which one are you?

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:20.370
I think you can tell that
if you look at my form.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.160
Hel.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:26.830
So it looks like we can
consider you fully recovered.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:31.460
Uh-huh, thanks to Father. This time--

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:32.880
I'll defeat you.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:33.880
Huh?

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:38.720
And without fail,
I'll fulfill Alicia's wish.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:45.350
No, without fail you're going to die here.
You can't save that girl.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:00.910
You're so desperate it's laughable.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:04.200
You want that badly to
recover Her Ladyship, eh?

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.330
Her Ladyship?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.870
Did you realize?

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:13.210
This body is built a little differently
than those of the other SPES leaders.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:18.970
Originally it was ordinary, human.
But because of this body's peculiarity,

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:21.590
it had a variety of experiments
performed on it...

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:26.310
Pain, heat, pain, heat... torment.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:30.980
Apparently, Her Ladyship
suffered some very harsh trials.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:34.730
And then one day, when she could
no longer endure that agony,

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.110
Her Ladyship brought me into being.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.490
So that's the story.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.910
A secondary secret personality
that Alicia generated

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.870
when she couldn't stand the agony
anymore... that's what Hel is.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:54.670
Half in anguish, half in sorrow--
that's how we lived life.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:12:01.130
If that's the case, I'll end both the anguish
and the sorrow for you right now.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.770
Kimi... zuka...

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:11.690
Alicia!

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:13.020
Don't.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:22.030
If you'd shot me through the heart
or the head, you would've won.

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.990
So Her Ladyship is that important to you.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:30.410
But such a soft-hearted bunch
won't defeat me.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:45.010
What is that?

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.260
Well, we are in the enemy's stronghold.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:51.520
I see. You're saying even something
like this was within your expectations.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:54.890
This time I'll finish you!

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.080
Sidekick, you're in the way.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.250
That's absurd.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.140
I'll kill you, and this time,

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:34.770
I'll fulfill my mission
as a member of SPES!

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:37.900
Ah. So it <i>was </i>a lie.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:44.780
What was? What about me
are you saying was a lie?

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:46.740
That you're a wholly new being,

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:50.990
brought into existence by
Alicia's self-protection instincts.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:55.660
The one who first took on SPES's
abilities and intentions was Alicia.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:14:03.300
So you were trying desperately to get
close to SPES. You're a mere impostor.

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:13.890
To what purpose would I do that?

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:17.140
What's the reason I've devoted
myself so entirely to SPES?

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:22.520
Most likely you wanted
to be loved... by a father.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:28.360
You only wanted a father to love you.
You wanted someone to appreciate you.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:29.490
That was all.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:34.240
You're wrong! You're wrong!

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:43.670
Earlier, your changing over to Alicia's
personality was to cause Alicia pain.

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:47.720
That's because you were envious of Alicia.

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:48.970
What are you saying?

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:51.430
You brought yourself as much
suffering as you possibly could,

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:55.600
yet you hated Alicia for finding
companions in Sidekick and me...

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:59.440
Hated her and envied her.

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.060
You're wrong!

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:04.150
You're wrong! You're wrong! You're wrong!

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:09.030
I'm not wrong. You only wanted to
be loved. You wanted companionship.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:13.490
Shut up! Kill one another.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.080
Siesta, you're not going to die.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:25.250
Sidekick, neither are you.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.420
Huh?

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.310
How?

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:45.770
It's simple. It's because I trust Sidekick
more than I trust anyone, even myself.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:52.070
We trust each other more than we trust
ourselves. That's all there is to it.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.620
What nonsense is that?

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.740
You're saying because of something
like that my power doesn't work?

00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:00.120
Isn't that a little too
convenient for you?

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.670
I'd ask you to at least
call it a spiritual bond.

00:16:02.670 --> 00:16:07.340
A spiritual bond? How can...?
How can such a thing...?

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:11.340
Hel, you don't need to conform
to some Sacred Writ.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.260
You don't need to kill
any more people either.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:17.220
You can have companionship
without doing those things.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:21.430
Spiritual bonds come into being.
Thus, you don't need to force yourself

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.400
to obey whatever he--
whatever Seed--tells you.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:25.560
So you say!

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:28.110
I can't lose.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:31.820
I'll admit it: I wanted to be loved.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.990
I wanted to be needed.

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:37.200
I wanted someone to acknowledge
that my being born meant something.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:41.450
It can't be just anybody, though.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:47.290
I live, fight, and lay ruin to the
world only for Father's sake.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:51.010
That's what my survival
instinct drives me to.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:55.590
Well and good. Shall we bring
this to a conclusion now?

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:57.970
Let's end it here.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.400
What now?

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.290
Sidekick!

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:40.060
Mom...

00:17:54.400 --> 00:18:00.240
It was supposed to be confined to the lab;
maybe the scent of food lured it out?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:07.580
Siesta!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:15.260
I want you to not move for a moment.

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:22.180
I've lost a little too much blood.

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:31.230
I need to exchange it for a new one...

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:41.910
Don't! If you want a heart,
I'll give you mine! Just don't...

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.700
Just not Siesta!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:49.830
I told you before that you'd
become my partner someday.

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:54.630
So we need to keep you alive, right?

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:04.970
I'll take the legendary
detective's heart for myself.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:12.480
At last, I've acquired a heart
that's worthy of this body.

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:15.150
With this, Father will certainly...

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:19.490
Give it back.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:27.950
That heart belongs to Siesta.
You're going to give it back!

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:32.750
That's an impossible proposition.
This belongs to me now.

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:36.130
Don't touch Siesta with your filthy hands!

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:41.550
Your fist won't reach me.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:49.350
Where is that rage welling up from?

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:53.900
What's the reason for that spiritual bond
that you both were talking about?

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:57.780
What on earth were you to her?

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:04.990
Hel's asking was immaterial;
I'd been thinking about this all along...

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:12.170
What on earth was I to Siesta?
What did I mean to her?

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.580
And yet...

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:18.460
...at this point, I can never know.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:29.810
Nevertheless... from that day we first
met, 10,000 meters up in the sky,

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:33.310
we continued our travels
over the course of three years.

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:36.060
During those days, which could
never be called tranquil,

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.110
my life was in jeopardy countless times.

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:42.780
I was denounced as stupid,
and pushed into absurd situations.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:49.490
And yet, in the midst of those thousand
absurdities, I laughed 10,000 times.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:52.210
I laughed together with Siesta.

00:20:55.670 --> 00:21:00.880
You ask what the relationship
was between Siesta and me?

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:06.050
You ask me what I thought of Siesta?

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:09.470
I knew that beyond a doubt,
from the beginning,

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:13.850
she was the most important thing
in the whole world to me!

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.990
What the...?

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:48.140
Sies... ta...

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.080
What just happened?

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:46.960
"Episode 10"
"So I Can't Become a Detective"
